Addresses performance feedback from #11418 on nested filter operation when excluding already-registered models from autoconfigured models list.

### Changes

Replaced O(n*m) nested `Array.some()` filter with O(n+m) Set-based lookup in `showConfigurationDialog()`:

```typescript
// Before: O(n*m) - nested iteration
const autoconfiguredModels = getAutoconfiguredModels()
  .filter(m => !registeredModels.some(rm => rm.provider === m.provider));

// After: O(n+m) - Set lookup
const registeredProviderIds = new Set(registeredModels?.map(rm => rm.provider));
const autoconfiguredModels = getAutoconfiguredModels()
  .filter(m => !registeredProviderIds.has(m.provider));
```

Improvement is most significant when both registered and autoconfigured model counts are high.

