### Intent

This PR improves how modal React components are rendered.

### Details

To start, everything to do with modal React rendering (`positronModalReactRenderer`, `positronModalDialog`, and `positronModalPopup`) and the Positron Data Explorer (`positronDataExplorer`, `positronDataGrid`, and supporting components) has been moved from `vs/base/browser/ui` to `vs/workbench/browser`. This was done because modal React rendering cannot function without access to the `IKeybindingsService`, which isn't available in `vs/base/browser/ui`.

With this refactoring, the `positronModalReactRenderer` class has access to the the `IKeybindingsService`, so the  `StopCommandsKeyEventProcessor` class was no longer needed. It and the `IKeyEventProcessor` interface were removed.

Prior to this PR, modal React rendering was based on an async / await design pattern. This approach was suboptimal because it required a lot of boilerplate code to set up the `Promise` and resolve it in the modal React component.

After this PR, modal React rendering has been simplified to a callback (when necessary) design pattern which can often be accomplished using only two lines of code.

For example, here's the confirmation modal dialog:

```TypeScript
/**
 * Shows the confirmation modal dialog.
 * @param keybindingService The keybinding service.
 * @param layoutService The layout service.
 * @param title The title.
 * @param message The message.
 * @param action The action to perform.
 */
export const confirmationModalDialog = async (
	keybindingService: IKeybindingService,
	layoutService: IWorkbenchLayoutService,
	title: string,
	message: string,
	action: () => Promise<void>
) => {
	// Create the modal React renderer.
	const renderer = new PositronModalReactRenderer({
		keybindingService,
		layoutService,
		container: layoutService.activeContainer
	});

	// Show the confirmation modal dialog.
	renderer.render(
		<OKCancelModalDialog
			renderer={renderer}
			width={400}
			height={195}
			title={title}
			onAccept={async () => {
				renderer.dispose();
				await action();
			}}
			onCancel={() => renderer.dispose()}>
			<VerticalStack>
				<div>{message}</div>
			</VerticalStack>
		</OKCancelModalDialog>
	);
};
```

A message modal dialog box can be further simplified to:

```TypeScript
/**
 * Shows a message modal dialog.
 * @param keybindingService The keybinding service.
 * @param layoutService The layout service.
 * @param title The title.
 * @param message The message.
 */
export const showMessageModalDialog = async (
	keybindingService: IKeybindingService,
	layoutService: IWorkbenchLayoutService,
	title: string,
	message: string
) => {
	// Create the modal React renderer.
	const renderer = new PositronModalReactRenderer({
		keybindingService,
		layoutService,
		container: layoutService.activeContainer
	});

	// Show the message modal dialog.
	renderer.render(
		<OKModalDialog
			renderer={renderer}
			width={400}
			height={195}
			title={title}
			onAccept={async () => {
				renderer.dispose();
			}}
			<VerticalStack>
				<div>{message}</div>
			</VerticalStack>
		</OKModalDialog>
	);
};
```

Another example: This is how the `DeleteAllVariablesModalDialog` is rendered now:

```TypeScript
// Create the renderer.
const renderer = new PositronModalReactRenderer({
	keybindingService: props.keybindingService,
	layoutService: props.layoutService,
	container: props.layoutService.activeContainer
});

// Show the delete all variables modal dialog.
renderer.render(
	<DeleteAllVariablesModalDialog
		renderer={renderer}
		deleteAllVariablesAction={async deleteAllVariablesResult =>
			positronVariablesContext.activePositronVariablesInstance?.requestClear(
				deleteAllVariablesResult.includeHiddenObjects
			)
		}
	/>
);
```

The `DeleteAllVariablesModalDialog` component now looks like any other functional component that accepts props and calls a callback:

```TypeScript
/**
 * DeleteAllVariablesResult interface.
 */
export interface DeleteAllVariablesResult {
	includeHiddenObjects: boolean;
}

/**
 * DeleteAllVariablesModalDialogProps interface.
 */
interface DeleteAllVariablesModalDialogProps {
	renderer: PositronModalReactRenderer;
	deleteAllVariablesAction: (result: DeleteAllVariablesResult) => Promise<void>;
}

/**
 * DeleteAllVariablesModalDialog component.
 * @param props The component properties.
 * @returns The component.
 */
export const DeleteAllVariablesModalDialog = (props: DeleteAllVariablesModalDialogProps) => {
	// Render.
	return (
		<OKCancelModalDialog
			renderer={props.renderer}
			width={375}
			height={175}
			title={localize('positron.deleteAllVariablesModalDialogTitle', "Delete All Variables")}
			okButtonTitle={localize('positron.yes', "Yes")}
			cancelButtonTitle={localize('positron.no', "No")}
			onAccept={async () => {
				props.renderer.dispose();
				await props.deleteAllVariablesAction({
					includeHiddenObjects: false
				});
			}}
			onCancel={() => props.renderer.dispose()}
		>
			<VerticalStack>
				<div>
					{localize(
						'positron.deleteAllVariablesModalDialogText',
						"Are you sure you want to delete all variables? This operation cannot be undone."
