This PR enables runtimes to participate in the `OpenerService` to open resource URIs that they support.

**`src/vs/workbench/api/common/positron/extHost.positron.protocol.ts`**

A new method called `$openResource` has been added to the `ExtHostLanguageRuntimeShape` interface.

```TypeScript
$openResource(handle: number, resource: URI | string): Promise<boolean>;
```

**`src/positron-dts/positron.d.ts`**

A new, optional method called `openResource` has been added to the `LanguageRuntime` interface. This method should be implemented by runtimes that can open resource URIs.

```TypeScript
/**
 * Opens a resource in the runtime.
 * @param resource The resource to open.
 * @returns true if the resource was opened; otherwise, false.
 */
openResource?(resource: vscode.Uri | string): Thenable<boolean>;
```

**`extensions/positron-r/src/runtime.ts`**

The `RRuntime` class implements the `openResource` method of the `LanguageRuntime` interface, allowing it to open resource URI's. At the moment, this method is stubbed out with support for `x-r-help` and `x-r-vignette` URI schemes:

```TypeScript
/**
 * Opens a resource in the runtime.
 * @param resource The resource to open.
 * @returns true if the resource was opened; otherwise, false.
 */
openResource(resource: vscode.Uri | string): Thenable<boolean> {
	// If the resource is a string, parse it as a URI.
	if (typeof resource === 'string') {
		resource = vscode.Uri.parse(resource);
	}

	// Dispatch the open.
	switch (resource.scheme) {
		// Help resource.
		case 'x-r-help':
			console.log('*******************************************************');
			console.log(`R runtime should open help resource "${resource.path}"`);
			console.log('*******************************************************');
			return Promise.resolve(true);

		// Vignette resource.
		case 'x-r-vignette':
			console.log('*******************************************************');
			console.log(`R runtime should open vignette resource "${resource.path}"`);
			console.log('*******************************************************');
			return Promise.resolve(true);

		// Unhandled.
		default:
			return Promise.resolve(false);
	}
}
```

_Another member of the team will be implementing code that opens `x-r-help` and `x-r-vignette` resource URIs._

**`src/vs/workbench/services/languageRuntime/common/languageRuntime.ts`**

The `LanguageRuntimeService` now implements the `IOpener` interface and adds itself as an opener in the `OpenerService`. When the `OpenerService` is opening a resource URI, each running runtime that implements the `openResource` method will get a crack at opening the resource.

**`extensions/positron-r/resources/scripts/startup.R`**

Finally, on startup, the `positron-r` extension now enables the `cli.hyperlink_help` and `cli.hyperlink_vignette` options.

```R
options(cli.hyperlink_help = TRUE)
options(cli.hyperlink_vignette = TRUE)
```

This allows `.help` and `.vignette` hyperlinks to be used in the R runtime:

```R
cli::cli_text("Help on Abort {.help rlang::abort}")
cli::cli_text("{.vignette dplyr::grouping}")
```

