### Background

The PositronProxy extension will offer two types of proxy servers: One for use by the Help feature and one for use by the Preview feature (at the moment, only the Help proxy server exists).

As this work progresses, we will be writing a lot of JavaScript code that will be injected into Help and Preview documents by their respective proxy servers.

We need a sane way to author this JavasScript. This PR addresses this issue.

(It also contains some general refactoring in the Help system and fixes so that external URLs now open using the OpenerService.)

#### The Old Way

Prior to this PR, any script code that was to be injected by a proxy server was written in a string constant in the `positronProxy.ts` file. For example, this was the first script that was injected by the Help proxy server:

```
...

// The script to inject.
const script = `<script>
(function() {
	var links = document.links;
	for (let i = 0; i < links.length; i++) {
		links[i].onclick = (e) => {
			window.parent.postMessage({
				command: "open-url",
				href: links[i].href
			}, "*");
			return false;
		};
	}
})();
</script>`;

...

// Inject the script.
let response = responseBuffer.toString('utf8');
response = response.replace('</body>', `${script}</body>`);
```

Obviously, this is really awful and things will get out of hand as the size and complexity of the scripts being injected increases.

#### The New Way

With this PR, scripts are now authored in the `resources/scripts.html` file:

<img width="808" alt="image" src="https://github.com/rstudio/positron/assets/853239/8ead3607-b700-47fa-8c0d-98f8b00fbddf">

This means that you get all the goodies you want like code completion, syntax checking, and so on, when you're writing the script code.

At runtime, these scripts are loaded from the `resources/scripts.html` file using JSDOM. They are then injected by the proxy server where needed. This is quite simple:

```
// Load the resources/scripts.html file.
const scriptsPath = path.join(this.context.extensionPath, 'resources', 'scripts.html');
const jsdom = new JSDOM(fs.readFileSync(scriptsPath));
const document = jsdom.window.document;

// Load the scripts from within the file.
this.helpHeaderScript = document.querySelector('#help-header-script')?.outerHTML;
```

